TEST 20930 -- IPv6 Static Multicast Routing - Interop with Static MLD
===========================================================================
Run:    2026-09-24 (~15:30-15:45 NZST), tb470
Build:  awplus_main-20260923-20
DUT:    IE520 3-member VCStack "IE520-stk"
Case:   ATKK Topology_A2, TestInt1 upstream, TestInt2-TestInt4 downstream, Ixia. Procedure
        (translated): 3. send multicast from TestInt1, confirm TestInt2-4 receive it;
        4. confirm the route is registered (show ip mroute); 5. send MLD Done from
        TestInt2-4, confirm they STILL receive it ("static group, so it is not deleted").
Setup:  as 38144.log (same session), PIM removed so the static route is the only forwarder:
      upstream    tb470 eth3 -> port3.0.9  vlan30  (source fd32:b1f0:dff8:d703::1)
      downstream  tb470 eth1 -> port3.0.13 vlan20
      downstream  tb470 eth2 -> IE520-sa port1.0.2 -> sa3 -> vlan1
  Two downstream VLANs rather than the case's three (the bench has three host NICs).
  Group ff1e::1:600; 20 frames per burst from eth3, hop limit 16, counted on the wire.
  IE520-sa's MLD snooping was turned off on its vlan1 for this case only, so that the SA's
  own snooping could not decide what reaches eth2. It was restored afterwards (below).
  (Replaces the 2026-09-22 UNMEASURED "needs more hosts".)

VERDICT: PASS -- the static route forwards to both downstream VLANs with no host joined, and
         keeps forwarding after both hosts send MLD leaves.

CONFIG (DUT)
  interface vlan1/vlan20/vlan30: no ipv6 pim sparse-mode   (ipv6 multicast-routing stays on)
  ipv6 multicast route fd32:b1f0:dff8:d703::1 ff1e::1:600 vlan30 vlan1,vlan20
  interface vlan20: ipv6 mld static-group ff1e::1:600
  interface vlan1:  ipv6 mld static-group ff1e::1:600

STEP 0 -- baseline, PIM off, no static route, no joins
      eth1 0/20, eth2 0/20

STEP 3 -- send from the upstream -> both downstreams receive (no host has joined)
      eth1 20/20, eth2 20/20
      show ipv6 mld groups: ff1e::1:600 on vlan20 (port3.0.13) and on every vlan1 port,
      Expires "stopped", Last Reporter "::" (static)

STEP 4 -- the route is registered in the table
      show ipv6 mroute:
        (fd32:b1f0:dff8:d703::1, ff1e::1:600), Owner IMI, Flags: F
          Incoming interface: vlan30
          Outgoing interface list: vlan1, vlan20
      show hsl fib (hardware):
        Group (ff1e::1:600) Source (fd32:b1f0:dff8:d703::1)  L2 L3 Entry, Mirror To CPU: No
          L3 IIf = 330; L3 outgoing 301 (vlan1), 320 (vlan20)
        IPv6 (S,G) Forwarding Entries: 1

STEP 5 -- the downstream hosts send MLD Done -> they still receive
  eth1 and eth2 join ff1e::1:600, then leave (socket close). The tb470 kernel speaks MLDv2,
  so its "Done" is a CHANGE_TO_INCLUDE {} record. Captured leaving each NIC (to ff02::16):
      eth1: +0.0s CHANGE_TO_EXCLUDE (join), +0.3s join, +7.6s CHANGE_TO_INCLUDE (leave), +8.2s leave
      eth2: +0.0s CHANGE_TO_EXCLUDE (join), +0.4s join, +7.6s CHANGE_TO_INCLUDE (leave), +7.9s leave
      while joined:            eth1 20/20, eth2 20/20
      8 s after the leaves:    eth1 20/20, eth2 20/20
      show ipv6 mld groups after the leaves:
        ff1e::1:600  vlan20 (port3.0.13)  00:02:38  stopped  fe80::3f84:db77:9294:e805 (eth1)
        ff1e::1:600  vlan1 (sa3)          00:02:33  stopped  fe80::cfe7:b827:c695:6034 (eth2)
        -- the entries still stand, uptime NOT reset by the leave
      show ipv6 mroute: unchanged (Owner IMI, in vlan30, out vlan1 + vlan20)

NOTES
  - Adding the downstreams one line at a time is refused. A second
    "ipv6 multicast route <S> <G> vlan30 vlan1" answers "% Static multicast route already
    exists for fd32:b1f0:dff8:d703::1, ff1e::1:600". All downstreams go in ONE command
    ("vlan1,vlan20" was accepted, and it is stored that way in running-config).
  - "ipv6 mld static-group" with no "interface" parameter installs the group on EVERY port
    of the VLAN in show ipv6 mld groups. On vlan1 that includes sa2, sa3 and the port2.0.x
    range of member 2, which is provisioned ("switch 2 provision ie520-28") but absent (the
    stack is members 1/3/4). Observed; not graded.
  - The first attempt's leave capture used BPF "icmp6", which cannot match MLD (it sits
    behind a hop-by-hop header), so step 5 was repeated with the capture above. The traffic
    counts were the same in both runs.
  - IE520-sa after the case: "ipv6 mld snooping" restored on vlan1 (running-config no
    longer shows "no ipv6 mld snooping").
